<div class="WordSection1"><h1>AGREED-UPON PROCEDURES REPORT ON PHYSICAL VERIFICATION OF INVENTORY</h1>
<p class="c i" style="font-size:9.5pt">(Special assignment under SRS 4400 (Revised), Agreed-Upon Procedures Engagements)</p><br>
<p style="text-align:left">To<br>The Board of Directors<br>Demo Hardware &amp; Paints Pvt Ltd</p>
<h2>1. Purpose</h2><p>We have performed the procedures agreed with you and listed below on the physical stock of Demo Hardware &amp; Paints Pvt Ltd as on 31 March 2026. The procedures were performed solely to help you find out whether the stock in the stock register is physically present at the recorded locations, in usable condition, and moving.</p>
<h2>2. Responsibilities</h2><p>Management is responsible for maintaining the stock register, its locations and the custody of stock, and has agreed that the procedures are appropriate for the purpose. We carried out the engagement in accordance with SRS 4400 (Revised) issued by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India and complied with the relevant ethical requirements.</p>
<h2>3. Procedures performed and findings</h2><table class="t" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4"><tr><th>No.</th><th>Procedure performed</th><th>Findings</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Obtained from management the item-wise stock register as on the verification date, showing item, brand, category, unit, book quantity, rate, last movement date and location (building, floor, room / godown, rack, shelf / bin).</td><td>Stock register of 36 items with book value ₹31,66,300, kept in 3 buildings, 8 rooms / godowns and 27 racks / bays. See Annexure A.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Physically counted the items at their recorded locations in the presence of the client's storekeeper. Counts were taken manually or from photographs counted by the tool and confirmed by our team; each photograph was kept with its SHA-256 fingerprint and time of count.</td><td>35 items with book value ₹31,35,100 were counted (99.0% of book value). 3 item(s) were counted from photographs.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Compared the physical quantity with the book quantity for each item counted and worked out the difference in value at the book rate.</td><td>Matched: 19; shortage: 12; excess: 3; not found: 1; not counted: 1. Shortage ₹1,73,100, excess ₹2,850, net difference -₹1,70,250. See Annexure B.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Compared the place where each item was found with the location in the stock register.</td><td>2 item(s) were found at a location different from the register. See Annexure C.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Inspected the condition of the stock and recorded the quantity seen as damaged.</td><td>Damaged stock seen: book value ₹75,520. See Annexure D.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Identified items with no movement for more than the agreed number of days, from the last movement date in the register.</td><td>No movement for more than 365 days: ₹5,63,600; between 180 and 365 days: ₹1,01,400. See Annexure E.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Listed shortages on costly items, shortages of 10% or more, and items not found, for management to check.</td><td>6 item(s) listed for management to check (marked in Annexure B).</td></tr></table>
<h2>4. No assurance</h2><p>The procedures performed are not an audit or a review, and we therefore do not express an opinion or any assurance on the stock or the stock register. Had we performed additional procedures, other matters might have come to our attention that would have been reported to you. Counts relate to the date and time stated and to the stock that was shown to us. Shortages are differences to be checked and do not by themselves indicate theft.</p>
<h2>5. Restriction on use</h2><p>This report is solely for the purpose stated in paragraph 1 and for your information. It is not to be used for any other purpose or given to any other party without our prior written consent.</p><br>
<p><b>For CA Debashis Pattnaik</b><br>Chartered Accountant</p><br><br><br>
<p>(CA Debashis Pattnaik)<br>Membership No.: 316339<br>UDIN: ______________________<br>Place: Bhubaneswar<br>Date: 28-11-2026</p></div>
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always;mso-break-type:section-break">
