<h2>Annexure E — Non-moving and slow-moving stock</h2><table class="t" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4"><tr><th>Item</th><th>Location</th><th>Days since movement</th><th>Class</th><th>Book value</th></tr><tr><td>Mixer Motor 5 HP (spare)</td><td>Showroom Block › First Floor › Store Room › R-02 › S-1</td><td class="n">700</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹74,000</td></tr><tr><td>Bathroom Tap – Chrome</td><td>Showroom Block › Ground Floor › Showroom › R-09 › S-2</td><td class="n">520</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹1,09,200</td></tr><tr><td>Welding Rod 3.15 mm</td><td>Showroom Block › First Floor › Store Room › R-04 › S-3</td><td class="n">450</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹32,000</td></tr><tr><td>MCB 32 A</td><td>Showroom Block › Ground Floor › Showroom › R-07 › S-1</td><td class="n">400</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹68,200</td></tr><tr><td>Synthetic Enamel 1 L – Red</td><td>Main Warehouse › First Floor › Godown B › R-02 › S-3</td><td class="n">400</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹61,200</td></tr><tr><td>HDPE Bag 25 kg</td><td>Main Warehouse › First Floor › Godown D › R-03 › S-4</td><td class="n">400</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹27,000</td></tr><tr><td>Titanium Dioxide</td><td>Main Warehouse › Ground Floor › Godown C › R-03 › Pallet 4</td><td class="n">380</td><td>Non-moving (> 365 days)</td><td class="n">₹1,92,000</td></tr><tr><td>Printed Label Roll</td><td>Main Warehouse › First Floor › Godown D › R-04 › S-1</td><td class="n">260</td><td>Slow-moving (180–365 days)</td><td class="n">₹31,200</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Primer 20 L</td><td>Main Warehouse › First Floor › Godown B › R-02 › S-1</td><td class="n">210</td><td>Slow-moving (180–365 days)</td><td class="n">₹70,200</td></tr></table>
<h2>Annexure F — Points for management</h2><p class="i" style="font-size:9pt">(Suggestions arising from the work; not findings under the agreed-upon procedures.)</p><h3>Summary</h3><p>35 of 36 items were counted, covering 99% of the book value of ₹31,66,300. Net difference is -₹1,70,250 (shortage ₹1,73,100, excess ₹2,850). 1 item(s) were not found, 2 item(s) were kept at another place, and 6 item(s) need to be checked.</p><h3>Points for management</h3><ol><li><b>Shortage of ₹1,73,100</b> in 13 items. Largest at Showroom Block › First Floor › Store Room (₹75,640); Showroom Block › First Floor › Strong Room (₹25,200). Possible reasons: sales or issues not entered, goods sent for repair, counting or unit errors, or loss. <i>Action:</i> check issue slips, challans and bills after the count date, recount, and adjust the books after approval.</li><li><b>2 item(s) were kept at a place other than the register.</b> Stock was shifted without updating the location. <i>Action:</i> update building / floor / godown / rack in the software and put labels on racks and bins.</li><li><b>Excess stock of ₹2,850.</b> Possible reasons: purchases or sales returns not entered, or goods of others kept in the godown. <i>Action:</i> match with goods receipt notes and supplier bills.</li><li><b>Damaged stock of ₹75,520.</b> Stock is valued at cost or realisable value, whichever is lower. <i>Action:</i> keep damaged goods separately, find their sale value and write down the difference.</li><li><b>Non-moving stock of ₹5,63,600</b> and slow-moving stock of ₹1,01,400. <i>Action:</i> plan clearance or return to supplier, and consider a provision.</li><li><b>6 costly or large-shortage item(s) to be checked.</b> <i>Action:</i> restrict access to the strong room and store room, CCTV at entry points, and surprise counts.</li></ol><h3>Suggestions for better stock control</h3><ol><li>Keep building, floor, godown, rack and bin for every item in the software and label the racks.</li><li>Keep bin cards for costly items and match them monthly.</li><li>Count one godown every quarter with this tool, so differences are found early.</li></ol>
<p>Suggested provision for damaged and old stock, for management's consideration: ₹1,57,510 (on the percentages set in the tool; to be confirmed against realisable values).</p></div></body></html>